From: RGOS <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] package/ruby: don't build the fiddle ext for host-ruby

ruby 4.x makes an ext that fails to configure fatal ("Fix the problems,
then remove these directories"), and host-ruby has no libffi dependency
to configure fiddle against. WebKitGTK only needs host-ruby as a build
tool; skip the ext the same way the target build does for MIPS
(--with-out-ext=fiddle).
---
 package/ruby/ruby.mk | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/package/ruby/ruby.mk
+++ b/package/ruby/ruby.mk
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ HOST_RUBY_CONF_OPTS = \
 	--disable-install-doc \
 	--disable-yjit \
 	--disable-zjit \
-	--with-out-ext=curses,readline \
+	--with-out-ext=curses,readline,fiddle \
 	--without-gmp
 
 ifeq ($(BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_LIBATOMIC),y)
